  "goodToKnow": "Hinreichend means sufficient, and it's formal: hinreichende Beweise, ein hinreichender Tatverdacht (sufficient suspicion to bring charges, a key legal term). In maths and logic, notwendig und hinreichend means necessary and sufficient. The everyday word is ausreichend, which is also the German school grade 4 (pass). Hinreichend bekannt means well enough known, often ironic. From hinreichen (to suffice)."
